nodes.body:
The code change is fine, but the comment is bad. Going into so much depth about pointer aliasing makes me think the fix is to tag the arguments with `__restrict__`. The motivation for only loading global memory once should be obvious for anyone who knows CUDA.
```suggestion
    // Get scalars from global memory
    const float lr = *lr_ptr;
    const float inv_scale = *inv_scale_ptr;
    const bool write_unscaled_grads = inv_scale != 1.0f;
```
Honestly it's clear enough without a comment.

